      ]
     },
     "rhs": 0.0
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "eqweather_scm_dynamics_step1410_derivative",
     "description": "The five dynamics components reading the ODE STATE instead of a frozen dumped column, at the state of WRF step 1410. Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4 build, dt = 60 s; data/eqwefic/scm_dyn) dumped by the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented, commit 83347b2 (rk_tendency, rk_step 1), merged with the same step's radiation subassembly dump and the wrfout eta grid (tools/merge_dumps.py -> data/eqwefic/dumps/dyn_column/esm_dump_dyn_suite_1410.json); the expected profiles are the same dumped mass-coupled increments divided by the coupling mass of their grid point that couplings/scm_dynamics_column.esm asserts, and the tolerances are that document's. What this test adds is the PATH: there the six state profiles reach the components as `const` data through the dumped template library, here they are the initial values of six ODE states, handed to the components through variable_map param_to_var edges into the additive coupling-target parameters the mount-edge libraries couplings/tests/scmstate_couple_*_inputs.esm lower input_u / input_v / input_w / input_theta_m / input_phi_p / input_qv to. Passing at the same tolerances is the statement that closing the loop changes no bit of the right-hand side. Only the base state (eta_w, phb, alb, pb, u_base, v_base, t_base, z_base) and the condensate in q_t still come from the dumped library, and all of those are time-invariant in this run. The total w tendency keeps its loose abs 1e-3 m/s^2 bound for the reason given in couplings/scm_dynamics_column.esm: WRF's single-precision p' carries 1.2-1.6e-2 Pa of rounding that g/(mu_d deta) ~ 0.016 m/s^2/Pa amplifies into a spurious w tendency the size of the physical one. Last assertion: The geopotential equation of a column with no coordinate vertical velocity is dphi/dt = g w exactly (ww == 0 identically for a horizontally uniform periodic column, PLAN.md 3.1), so this asserts the state document's phi' tendency against g times its own initial w with g taken from lib/wrf_constants.esm. The reference names the constant MODEL-QUALIFIED (EqWeatherScmDynamics.wrf.g) rather than by the bare mount name CLAUDE.md prescribes, because the bare form does not resolve in an assertion reference expression: the runner reports E_TREEWALK_UNBOUND_NAME for `wrf.g` there while accepting it in every equation of the same model. The drawback the bare form exists to avoid -- a component that can only be mounted under its own name -- does not apply to a top-level coupling document, which is never re-mounted -- an exact identity, hence the 1e-12 bound.",
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "mu_p0": -97.75,
