    {
     "id": "eqweather_scm_dynamics_step1410_acoustic_60s",
     "description": "A 60 s integration of the same state, which is what distinguishes this document from couplings/scm_dynamics_column.esm: the right-hand side is evaluated at a state the integrator produced, not at a dumped one. Three things are asserted, none of them a fitted number. (1) The undamped vertical acoustic mode stays BOUNDED. WRF removes it with the forward-backward acoustic sub-step and the off-centring parameter epssm; nothing here does, so the column rings at whatever amplitude its departure from float64 hydrostatic balance excites. Measured: max |w| over the column is 5.54e-4 m/s at t = 0, 9.60e-4 at t = 60 s and 9.35e-4 at t = 600 s, and max |dw/dt| falls from 5.40e-4 to 3.13e-4 m/s^2 -- the response is the size of the column's own w and does NOT grow, so the bounds here are abs 2e-3 m/s and abs 1e-3 m/s^2, about 2x and 3x the measured values. (2) theta_m in the lowest layer is UNCHANGED to the last bit: the only theta_m tendency in the dynamics half is the Rayleigh sponge, which is identically zero below z_top - zdamp = 6979 m, and layer 1 is at 25.8 m. Tolerance abs 0, and it passes. (3) u in the lowest layer has moved by its own asserted tendency: the expected value is the test-1 reference du_dt[1] = 4.2536e-4 m/s^2 times 60 s added to the dumped u[1], which ties the trajectory to the derivative test. Measured residual 7.4e-5 m/s against a bound of 2e-4, the difference being the second-order change of the tendency itself over the window. COST, measured on this machine: 18.0 s of wall time for this 60 s span and 164.9 s for a 600 s span -- close to linear, about 0.27 s of wall time per simulated second, so a single 24 h span of the dynamics half alone would take about 6.6 h. That, not the iteration cap of PLAN.md 3.1 gap (s), is what makes the checkpointed windows of item (5) necessary. ITEM (4) MEASURED HERE TOO, and it is not the lever it was expected to be. Replacing the dumped REAL*4 phi' with the profile that puts the column in EXACT float64 hydrostatic balance -- integrate dp'/ds = -(1 + q_m) mu' - q_m mu_b down from the lid, invert the equation of state for alpha_d, integrate alpha' up for phi' -- moves phi' by at most 0.050 m^2/s^2 (5.1 mm of interface height) and annihilates the vertical pressure-gradient-plus-buoyancy term to 3.3e-11 m/s^2 (the third test). Re-running the 600 s span from that state gives max |w| 6.81e-4 instead of 9.35e-4 (-27 %) and 125.7 s of wall time instead of 164.9 s (-24 %) -- while u, v and theta_m in the lowest layer agree with the unbalanced run to EIGHT significant figures (4.212193608 vs 4.212193614 m/s). So the rebalancing is thermodynamically free and removes a quarter of the ringing, but max |dw/dt| at t = 600 s is 2.77e-4 against 2.82e-4: by then the column has forgotten its initial condition and settled at its own acoustic level. The mode is a PERMANENT feature of the continuous equations, not an initial transient -- what WRF has and this document does not is the off-centring of its split-explicit acoustic sub-step (epssm), a property of the time scheme with no equation-level counterpart to transcribe.",
